(5748117, 808534, 8891, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Zoomdak:</b></div><hr/><i> I don''t believe this actually should have been disqualified. It was done in camera. Or is multi-exposure in-camera now off limits too? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Sorry about your DQ. Yeah, Multi Exposures in camera have been off limits even in advanced for quite a while. Apparently the feeling was to keep everyone on an even playing field since not all cams have the capability. I always wanted to try to do one on my Nikon D200 and never bothered because of the rule change.</td>', 'Originally posted by Zoomdak: I don''t believe this actually should have been disqualified. It was done in camera. Or is multi-exposure in-camera now off limits too?   Sorry about your DQ. Yeah, Multi Exposures in camera have been off limits even in advanced for quite a while. Apparently the feeling was to keep everyone on an even playing field since not all cams have the capability. I always wanted to try to do one on my Nikon D200 and never bothered because of the rule change.', '2009-12-01 09:39:53.000000', NULL, 0),
